Fourth, community engagement can expand

44
00:03:30.399 --> 00:03:35.397
the people, knowledge and resources
involved in learning. Fifth, partnerships

45
00:03:35.398 --> 00:03:40.067
grow through mutual trust, respect and
responsibility. We can show those

46
00:03:40.068 --> 00:03:44.605
qualities by listening carefully,
explaining clearly and doing what we

47
00:03:44.606 --> 00:03:49.472
agree to do. Sixth, partnership needs
committed, collaborative and creative

48
00:03:49.473 --> 00:03:54.077
leadership. Someone needs to make the time
and processes possible. In a

49
00:03:54.078 --> 00:03:58.878
meeting, these principles become visible
through a shared purpose, student

50
00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:03.943
communication, accessible information, and
clear next steps. Who will do what,

51
00:04:03.944 --> 00:04:09.007
and when will we check in again? Family
and school perspectives may differ. We

52
00:04:09.008 --> 00:04:14.269
can listen and show respect while we are
still working through those differences.

53
00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:19.663
Bringing those perspectives together from
the beginning gives us a better basis for

54
00:04:19.664 --> 00:04:21.044
deciding what to try.

55
00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:27.589
There are many points of collaboration
around an Autistic student: between

56
